\ snap.fam — the state from a snapshot (docs/NODE.md, step 6), after
\ connect.fam.  As tabminer's fast sync (miner/src/chain.rs's stage_part_in,
\ stage_name_part and finish_snapshot; net.rs's manifest and part
\ formats): the state after a block S, from its manifest and parts, each
\ checked, then the whole against S's state root and the coins issued to
\ S's height; S's own chain proof covers every block before it.
\
\ A manifest: the counter after S (u64), the root of each output part (a
\ subtree of 2^14 positions; a count and digests), the name trie's root,
\ and each name part's first key (15 bytes, big-endian) and hash (a count
\ and entries).  An output part: its unspent outputs (position u64,
\ commitment, memo, amount u64, creation height u32) ascending, then which
\ are commits (position, hash, height), ascending.  A name part: its
\ records, in key order.
\
\ snman ( m n hS -- code )  the manifest of the block with header hS.
\ snpart ( i p n -- code )  part i (outputs, then names), checked and
\ installed.
\ snfin ( hS -- code )  the state complete.  Codes: 0, -40 (tabminer's
\ BadSnapshot), or -10 for bytes that do not decode.
\ shdr ( h -- )  a header stored at its height (S's parent, for S's proof).
\ sverify ( hS body n -- flag )  S's body and chain proof, its statement's
\ first output position from the manifest's counter (snman first).

: snx variable ;  : snr variable ;  : sroots variable ;  : snroot variable ;  : snn variable ;  : snam variable ;
: sdone variable ;  : ssum variable ;  : sbig variable ;  : sents variable ;  : snent variable ;
: scom variable ;  : sncom variable ;  : slo variable ;  : sbh variable ;
: snxh variable ;  : spart variable ;  : sphi variable ;  : spcnt variable ;
: srecs variable ;  : snrec variable ;  : skey variable ;  : spk variable ;  : sval variable ;
: cla variable ;  : clc variable ;  : sbi variable ;  : sbn variable ;  : sba variable ;  : sbl variable ;  : skl variable ;  : skh variable ;  : spb variable ;  : spp variable ;  : sbk variable ;  : sbs variable ;

: sbad  FFFFFFD8 lit bfail ;                  \ -40
: sread  over + bq ! bp !  0 lit bcode ! ;           \ ( a n -- )  the reader on these bytes
: bu64  bu32 bu32 dup FF lit u> if bbad then ;   \ ( -- lo hi )  a counter or position (40 bits)
\ sparts ( -- n )  the output parts of the counter (snx, snxh): over 2^14,
\ rounded up.
: sparts  snx @ E lit rshift  snxh @ 12 lit lshift or  snx @ 3FFF lit and if 1 lit + then ;
: kcmp  4 lit wcmp ;                          \ ( a b -- c )  4-word keys
\ k15 ( a k -- )  the key k (4 words) from 15 big-endian bytes at a.
: k15  over 3 lit be@ over 3 lit w!  over 3 lit + 4 lit be@ over 2 lit w!  over 7 lit + 4 lit be@ over 1 lit w!  swap B lit + 4 lit be@ swap ! ;

\ climb ( a c from to -- )  the c digests at a, nodes at level `from` with
\ indexes 0 to c-1, climbed to level `to` (above `from`) in place: a pair's
\ parent is their compression, a missing sibling the empty subtree's.
: climb
rot clc ! rot cla !
swap do
	clc @ 1 lit + 1 lit rshift 0 lit do
		cla @ i 6 lit lshift +
		i 1 lit lshift 1 lit + clc @ u< if dup 20 lit + else j dfl then
		cla @ i 5 lit lshift + compress
	loop
	clc @ 1 lit + 1 lit rshift clc !
loop ;

: spe variable ;  : sel variable ;  : seh variable ;  : swf variable ;
: sca variable ;  : scb variable ;  : scn variable ;  : scm variable ;  : sci variable ;  : scj variable ;
: scl variable ;  : scp variable ;  : scq variable ;
: sce  24 lit * ;                             \ ( k -- off )  a node: its index, its digest
\ smerge ( l -- )  scb (scm nodes) = sca's (scn) with the parts at level l,
\ by index.
: smerge
scl !  0 lit scm !  0 lit sci !  0 lit scj !
begin
	begin scj @ snr @ u< if scj @ 30 lit * sroots @ + @ scl @ <> else 0 lit then while scj @ 1 lit + scj ! repeat
	sci @ scn @ u<  scj @ snr @ u<  or
while
	scj @ snr @ u< if
		sci @ scn @ u< if sci @ sce sca @ + @  scj @ 30 lit * sroots @ + 4 lit + @ u< else 0 lit then
	else -1 lit then
	if sci @ sce sca @ +  scm @ sce scb @ +  24 lit bcopy  sci @ 1 lit + sci !
	else
		scj @ 30 lit * sroots @ + dup 4 lit + @ scm @ sce scb @ + !  10 lit + scm @ sce scb @ + 4 lit + dle
		scj @ 1 lit + scj !
	then
	scm @ 1 lit + scm !
repeat ;
\ sparent ( l -- )  sca (scn nodes) = the parents of scb's (scm) at level l.
: sparent
scl !  0 lit scn !  0 lit sci !
begin sci @ scm @ u< while
	sci @ sce scb @ + scp !
	scp @ @ 1 lit rshift  scn @ sce sca @ + !
	scn @ sce sca @ + 4 lit + scq !
	scp @ @ 1 lit and if
		scl @ dfl  scp @ 4 lit +  scq @ compress  sci @ 1 lit + sci !
	else
		sci @ 1 lit + scm @ u< if scp @ 24 lit + @ scp @ @ 1 lit + = else 0 lit then
		if scp @ 4 lit +  scp @ 28 lit +  scq @ compress  sci @ 2 lit + sci !
		else scp @ 4 lit +  scl @ dfl  scq @ compress  sci @ 1 lit + sci ! then
	then
	scn @ 1 lit + scn !
repeat ;
\ scomp  stmd: the state root the parts and the name root compose to.
: scomp
snr @ 2 lit + sce dup malloc sca !  malloc scb !  0 lit scn !
27 lit E lit do i smerge i sparent loop
27 lit smerge
scm @ if scb @ 4 lit + else 27 lit dfl then  tmpa @ 8 lit wcopy
snroot @ tmpb @ dle  tmpa @ tmpb @ stmd @ compress  stmd @ dfrom
sca @ free  scb @ free ;
\ swell ( -- flag )  the output parts laid out as every node lays them out
\ (tabminer's Manifest::well_formed): subtrees of the output half from
\ level 14, below the counter, ascending and apart, holding 1 to 2^14
\ outputs each, each one's parent more.
: swell
sroots @ mob !  snr @ mon !  -1 lit swf !
snr @ ?dup if 0 lit do
	i ope @ dup E lit u< swap 27 lit u> or if 0 lit swf ! then
	i ope 8 lit + @ if 0 lit swf ! then
	swf @ if i ope 4 lit + @  27 lit i ope @ - rshift if 0 lit swf ! then then
	i ope C lit + @ dup 0= swap 4000 lit u> or if 0 lit swf ! then
	swf @ if i opf snx @ snxh @ p< 0= if 0 lit swf ! then then
	swf @ i 0= 0= and if i opf i 1 lit - ope2 p< if 0 lit swf ! then then
loop then
snr @ 1 lit + 2 lit lshift malloc mos !  0 lit mos @ 0 lit w!
snr @ ?dup if 0 lit do mos @ i w@ i ope C lit + @ + mos @ i 1 lit + w! loop then
swf @ if snr @ ?dup if 0 lit do
	i ope @ 27 lit u< if
		i ope @ 1 lit +  i ope 4 lit + @ 1 lit rshift
		2dup p40 wfh ! wfl !  1 lit + p40 weh ! wel !
		mohi mos @ swap w@  molo mos @ swap w@ -  4000 lit u> 0= if 0 lit swf ! then
	then
loop then then
mos @ free  0 lit mob !  0 lit mon !
swf @ ;

: snman  ( m n hS -- code )
sbh !  sread
sroots @ ?dup if free then  0 lit sroots !  0 lit snr !
bu64 snxh ! snx !
bu32 dup bleft 2D lit / u> if drop bbad 0 lit then dup snr !
30 lit * 30 lit + malloc sroots !
snr @ ?dup if 0 lit do bcode @ 0= if
	sroots @ i 30 lit * +
	1 lit btake c@ over !  bu32 over 4 lit + !  bu32 over 8 lit + !  bu32 over C lit + !
	20 lit btake dup 8 lit bcanon  over 10 lit + 20 lit bcopy  drop
then loop then
20 lit btake snroot !  bcode @ 0= if snroot @ 8 lit bcanon then
bu32 dup bleft 2F lit / u> if drop bbad 0 lit then dup snn !  2F lit * btake snam !
bcode @ 0= if snn @ ?dup if 0 lit do snam @ i 2F lit * + F lit + 8 lit bcanon loop then then
bcode @ 0= bp @ bq @ <> and if bbad then
bcode @ 0= if
	swell 0= if sbad then
	snn @ 1 lit u> if snn @ 1 lit do
		snam @ i 1 lit - 2F lit * + tmpa @ k15  snam @ i 2F lit * + tmpb @ k15
		tmpa @ tmpb @ kcmp 0 lit < 0= if sbad then
	loop then
then
bcode @ 0= if scomp  stmd @ sbh @ 4C lit + 8 lit wcmp if sbad then then
0 lit sdone !  ssum @ 4 lit wzero
bcode @ ;

\ srec ( e -- )  an output part's entry as a record in rb: commitment,
\ slot (memo and the amount's limbs), height.
: srec
dup 8 lit + rb @ 34 lit bcopy
dup 3C lit + le@ over 40 lit + le@
over 3FFFFFFF lit and rb @ 34 lit + !
over 1E lit rshift over 2 lit lshift or 3FFFFFFF lit and rb @ 38 lit + !
nip 1C lit rshift rb @ 3C lit + !
44 lit + le@ rb @ 40 lit + ! ;
: epos  48 lit * sents @ + le@ ;             \ ( k -- pos )
: epos2  48 lit * sents @ + dup le@ swap 4 lit + le@ ;    \ ( k -- lo hi )
\ sfind ( lo hi -- k | -1 )  the output at a position.
: sfind  FFFFFFFF lit -rot snent @ ?dup if 0 lit do 2dup i epos2 rot = -rot = and if rot drop i -rot then loop then 2drop ;

\ sin? ( lo hi -- flag )  in the part: from its first position to its end
\ or the counter.
: sin?  2dup slo @ sphi @ p< 0= -rot sel @ seh @ p< and ;

: snpout  ( i p n -- )
sread  spart !
\ the part: its subtree (the manifest's entry), below the counter
spart @ 30 lit * sroots @ + spe !
spe @ @  spe @ 4 lit + @  2dup p40 sphi ! slo !  1 lit + p40 seh ! sel !
snx @ snxh @ sel @ seh @ p< if snx @ sel !  snxh @ seh ! then
bu32 dup bleft 48 lit / u> if drop bbad 0 lit then dup snent !  48 lit * btake sents !
bcode @ 0= if snent @ ?dup if 0 lit do sents @ i 48 lit * + dup 4 lit + le@ FF lit u> if bbad then 8 lit + D lit bcanon loop then then
bu32 dup bleft 2C lit / u> if drop bbad 0 lit then dup sncom !  2C lit * btake scom !
bcode @ 0= if sncom @ ?dup if 0 lit do scom @ i 2C lit * + dup 4 lit + le@ FF lit u> if bbad then 8 lit + 8 lit bcanon loop then then
bcode @ 0= bp @ bq @ <> and if bbad then
\ as many as the manifest says; ascending, in the part
bcode @ 0= if snent @ spe @ C lit + @ <> if sbad then then
bcode @ 0= if snent @ ?dup if 0 lit do
	i epos2 sin? 0= if sbad then
	i if i 1 lit - epos2 i epos2 p< 0= if sbad then then
loop then then
\ each commit one of the outputs, holding its commit's leaf
bcode @ 0= if sncom @ ?dup if 0 lit do
	scom @ i 2C lit * + dup le@ swap 4 lit + le@ sin? 0= if sbad then
	scom @ i 2C lit * +  dup le@ over 4 lit + le@ sfind
	dup 0< if 2drop sbad else
		48 lit * sents @ + 8 lit +  swap dup 8 lit + swap 28 lit + le@ stmd @ cleaf
		stmd @ dfrom  stmd @ swap 8 lit wcmp if sbad then
	then
loop then then
\ installed, and its subtree's root, from the tree, the manifest's
bcode @ 0= if
	stfd @ 1 lit txbegin stx !
	0 lit ndirty !
	snent @ ?dup if 0 lit do
		i 48 lit * sents @ + dup srec  rb @ swap dup le@ swap 4 lit + le@ oput
		i 48 lit * sents @ + 3C lit + dup le@ swap 4 lit + le@ ssum @ amount+
	loop then
	sncom @ ?dup if 0 lit do
		scom @ i 2C lit * + dup 8 lit + cb @ 24 lit bcopy  dup le@ swap 4 lit + le@ kcommit cb @ 24 lit sput
	loop then
	sprop
	spe @ @  spe @ 4 lit + @  tmpa @ nget  tmpa @ dfrom  tmpa @ spe @ 10 lit + 8 lit wcmp if sbad then
	serr @ bcode @ or if serr @ if sbad then stx @ txabort drop else stx @ txcommit drop sdone @ 1 lit + sdone ! then
	0 lit ndirty !
then ;

\ ── Name parts (names.rs's part_hash) ──

\ sbucket ( k -- b )  a key's bucket: its top 16 bits.
: sbucket  3 lit w@ 8 lit rshift ;

: snpname  ( j p n -- )
sread  spk !
bu32 dup bleft 61 lit / u> if drop bbad 0 lit then snrec !
snrec @ 3 lit lshift 20 lit + malloc srecs !
snrec @ ?dup if 0 lit do bcode @ 0= if brec srecs @ i w! then loop then
bcode @ 0= bp @ bq @ <> and if bbad then
\ the part's keys, from its first to the next part's
spk @ 2F lit * snam @ + skl @ k15
spk @ 1 lit + snn @ u< if spk @ 1 lit + 2F lit * snam @ + skh @ k15 else skh @ 4 lit 0 lit do FFFFFFFF lit over i w! loop drop then
bcode @ 0= if
	snrec @ 4 lit lshift 10 lit + malloc skey !  snrec @ 5 lit lshift 20 lit + malloc sval !
	snrec @ ?dup if 0 lit do
		srecs @ i w@ sval @ i 5 lit lshift + rvalue  nkey @ skey @ i 4 lit lshift + 4 lit wcopy
		skey @ i 4 lit lshift +  dup skl @ kcmp 0< over skh @ kcmp 0< 0= or if sbad then
		i if dup 10 lit - over kcmp 0< 0= if sbad then then drop
	loop then
	\ the hash: per bucket, hash_domain 12 of the count and the records'
	\ bytes packed; then hash_domain 11 of each bucket and its hash
	snrec @ 9 lit * 20 lit + 2 lit lshift malloc spb !  spb @ spp !
	snrec @ if bp @ srecs @ @ - else 0 lit then 3 lit / 10 lit + 2 lit lshift malloc sbk !
	0 lit
	begin dup snrec @ u< while
		dup sbi !
		dup 4 lit lshift skey @ + sbucket sbs !
		dup begin 1 lit + dup snrec @ u< if dup 4 lit lshift skey @ + sbucket sbs @ = else 0 lit then 0= until nip
		dup sbi @ - sbn !
		sbs @ tom spp @ !  spp @ 4 lit + spp !
		sbn @ tom sbk @ !
		srecs @ sbi @ w@ sba !  srecs @ over 1 lit - w@ dup rsize + sba @ - sbl !
		sba @ sbl @ sbk @ 4 lit + pack3
		sbk @ sbl @ 2 lit + 3 lit / 1 lit + C lit spp @ hdom  spp @ 20 lit + spp !
	repeat drop
	spb @ spp @ spb @ - 2 lit rshift B lit stmd @ hdom  stmd @ dfrom
	stmd @ spk @ 2F lit * snam @ + F lit + 8 lit wcmp if sbad then
	spb @ free  sbk @ free
then
\ installed: each record, and its leaf in the trie
bcode @ 0= if
	stfd @ 1 lit txbegin stx !
	snrec @ ?dup if 0 lit do
		skey @ i 4 lit lshift + dup rtouch krec  srecs @ i w@ dup rsize sput
		skey @ i 4 lit lshift +  sval @ i 5 lit lshift + tinsert
	loop then
	serr @ if sbad stx @ txabort drop else stx @ txcommit drop sdone @ 1 lit + sdone ! then
	skey @ free  sval @ free
then
srecs @ free ;

: snpart  ( i p n -- code )
rot dup snr @ u< if -rot snpout else snr @ - -rot snpname then  bcode @ ;

\ issued ( h acc -- )  acc (4 words) = the coins issued by blocks 1 to h
\ (tabminer's ChainParams::issued): 1500 coins a block for the first era,
\ 500 for the second, 7 for the third.
: sac variable ;  : sma variable ;  : smb variable ;  : smc variable ;  : sih variable ;  : sis variable ;
: sera  ( n lo hi -- )  smb @ 1 lit w!  smb @ !  sma @ !  smc @ 4 lit wzero  sma @ 1 lit smb @ 2 lit smc @ wmul  sac @ smc @ sac @ 4 lit wadd drop ;
: issued
sac ! sih !  sac @ 4 lit wzero
sih @ 2CE98 lit umin  75ABF000 lit DA4 lit sera
sih @ 2CE98 lit u> if sih @ 2CE98 lit - 2CE98 lit umin  27395000 lit 48C lit sera then
sih @ 59D30 lit u> if sih @ 59D30 lit - 3220080 lit umin  4C533C00 lit 10 lit sera then ;

: snfin  ( hS -- code )
sbh !  0 lit bcode !
sdone @ snr @ snn @ + <> if sbad then
bcode @ 0= if
	stfd @ 1 lit txbegin stx !
	snx @ 70 lit mput  snxh @ 71 lit mput
	\ (each part's subtree built as it came, and the levels above it)
	tmpb @ troot  tmpb @ dfrom  tmpb @ snroot @ 8 lit wcmp if sbad then
	stmd @ sroot0  stmd @ sbh @ 4C lit + 8 lit wcmp if sbad then
	sbh @ 20 lit + @ sis @ issued  ssum @ sis @ 4 lit wcmp if sbad then
	sbh @ 20 lit + @ 68 lit mput  sbh @ 20 lit + @ khdr sbh @ CC lit sput
	\ its buckets, all, and its own manifest (manifest.fam): served too
	-1 lit rtall !  mbuckets  sroots @ snr @ mgiven  sbh @ 20 lit + @ snx @ snxh @ 0 lit msnap
	bcode @ serr @ or if stx @ txabort drop else stx @ txcommit drop then
	0 lit ndirty !
then
bcode @ ;

: shdr  ( h -- )
stfd @ 1 lit txbegin stx !  dup 20 lit + @ khdr swap CC lit sput  stx @ txcommit drop ;

: sverify  ( hS body n -- flag )
rot bh !  bh @ 20 lit + @ sh !  0 lit bcode !
bparse
bcode @ 0= if stmd @ bcommit  stmd @ dfrom  stmd @ bh @ 2C lit + 8 lit wcmp if FFFFFFF5 lit bfail then then
bcode @ 0= if
	0 lit bnops @ ?dup if 0 lit do bops @ i 3 lit lshift + @ 1 lit = if 1 lit + then loop then
	\ S's first position: the counter less what S made (40 bits)
	bnout @ +  dup snx @ swap - sfirst !  snx @ u> snxh @ swap if 1 lit - then sfirsth !
	snx @ sctr !  snxh @ sctrh !
	stfd @ 0 lit txbegin stx !  sproof  stx @ txcommit drop
else 0 lit then
bops @ free ;

\ sninit  the snapshot's scratch.
: sninit  20 lit alloc ssum !  20 lit alloc sis !  10 lit alloc skl !  10 lit alloc skh !  10 lit alloc sma !  10 lit alloc smb !  20 lit alloc smc ! ;
